title: A, but not B
mode: draw
chapter: Signals and gates
check: behaves
parts: and or not
---- intro
Gates mix well. Say you want a light that comes on when `a` is on **and `b` is off**. In words: "a AND (NOT b)".

| a | b | y |
|---|---|---|
| 0 | 0 | 0 |
| 0 | 1 | 0 |
| 1 | 0 | 1 |
| 1 | 1 | 0 |

A NOT gate on `b` turns "b is off" into a 1, and an AND joins it with `a`.
---- task
Make `y` light only when `a` is on and `b` is off.
---- start
input a 0 0
input b 0 80
led y 380 40
---- reference
input a, b
led y
y = a & ~b
---- answer
input a 0 0
input b 0 80
not n1 120 80
and g1 240 30
led y 380 40
a -> g1.0
b -> n1.in
n1 -> g1.1
g1 -> y
---- hint1
You need two gates: a NOT and an AND.
---- hint2
`b` goes into the NOT gate. The AND gate gets `a` and the NOT gate's output, and feeds `y`.
---- solution
NOT `b` is 1 exactly when `b` is off. ANDed with `a`, the light is on only for `a` on and `b` off.
---- done
Think of a machine that runs when you press start (`a`) but stops when a safety door (`b`) is open. Many real control circuits are this small.
